   "text": {
    "L1": "Papa searches everywhere for his spectacles, looking under the sofa and behind the door.",
    "L2": "He even searches the floor, but the poem saves its surprise for the end.",
    "L3": "The spectacles are on Papa’s head all along.",
    "L4": "That is funny because Mummy and we can see them, but Papa cannot.",
    "L5": "The poem has rhythm, so pause at the end of each line as you recite it.",
    "L6": "Words can rhyme by sound, even when their final letters differ: head and said rhyme.",
    "L7": "Here is a language point: spectacles is a pair-word, so we say, “Spectacles are.”",
    "L8": "We say “a pair of spectacles,” not “a spectacles.”"
   },
